{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% from "_macros.html.j2" import chart, key %}
{% block title %}Charts{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<h1>Charts</h1>
<p class="lead">Every measure for every system. Same data, same container limits, same query text apart from published
  mechanical dialect translation. The sections down to integration overhead use tables stored in the database;
  <a href="#parquet">Parquet entry points</a>, at the end, is a separate workload over Parquet files, never drawn on the same chart.</p>
{% if empty %}
{% include "_preview.html.j2" %}
{% else %}
{{ key() }}
<div class="controls" id="controls" data-controls="sf,systems,metric"></div>
<h2>Query speed</h2>
{{ chart("power_query", "Per-query time (s, log scale)", "One bar per system and query. Warm median of three warm runs, or the cold first run; toggle above.", 460, true) }}
<h2>Load and storage</h2>
<div class="grid">
{{ chart("load", "Load time (s)", "Bulk path is each system's fastest documented loader. Convert path starts from row-store tables and converts them; the staging load is in the tooltip.", 340) }}
{{ chart("storage", "Storage after load (bytes)", "Total data directory, with redo or WAL counted and replication logs excluded.", 340) }}
</div>
<h2>Concurrency</h2>
<div class="grid">
{{ chart("curve", "Throughput vs concurrent streams (qph)", "Warm cache; each stream runs the 22 queries once in its own order.", 340) }}
{{ chart("latency", "Query latency vs concurrent streams (p95, s)", "95th percentile over the successful queries.", 340) }}
</div>
<h2>SQL compatibility</h2>
<p class="note">A fixed probe suite of statements an OLTP application would try. The row-store baselines build the expected results, so only
  the integrations are shown. A probe that fails, or returns the same wrong result, on a plain row-store table of the
  same server is n/a (the host server itself does not support it), for every system alike; hover a cell for the reason.</p>
{{ chart("compat_summary", "Probe outcomes per system", "Each probe gets exactly one class. Share of probes.", 340) }}
{{ chart("compat_heatmap", "Probe by probe", "Letters repeat the colour: D ran in DuckDB, F row-path fallback, E error, ✗ wrong result, ? pushdown unobservable, ✓ DML/DDL ok (not scored), – n/a.", 600) }}
<h2>Silent slow paths</h2>
{{ chart("fallback", "Share of statements that quietly ran on the row path", "TPC-H queries and probes. A system that cannot show whether DuckDB ran a statement has no share (n/a), never 0%.", 340) }}
<h2>Integration overhead</h2>
{{ chart("overhead_query", "Per-query ratio to plain DuckDB at the same version (log scale)", "1x means as fast as plain DuckDB of the same version. n/a where no plain run exists at that version.", 420, true) }}
<div class="tablewrap" id="overhead_table"></div>
{% if parquet %}
<h2 id="parquet">Parquet entry points</h2>
<section class="card prose">
  <p>VillageSQL's <code>vsql_duckdb</code> is not a storage engine. It adds functions, <code>duckdb_query(sql)</code> and
    <code>duckdb_scalar(sql)</code>, that run DuckDB SQL verbatim over external files (Parquet, CSV, JSON) and return the
    result as a JSON string. Ordinary SQL on MySQL tables is never routed to DuckDB, and DuckDB cannot read InnoDB tables.
    Results are capped by <code>max_result_bytes</code> and <code>KILL QUERY</code> does not reach the embedded DuckDB.
    So the table-based measures above are n/a for it.</p>
  <p>That is a different design, not a lesser one, so it is measured on its own workload: TPC-H as local Parquet files, the
    22 queries sent through each system's raw DuckDB entry point, plus the JSON_TABLE join with an InnoDB table that
    VillageSQL documents. On the same files: plain DuckDB, pg_duckdb <code>duckdb.query()</code> and MariaDB
    <code>run_in_duckdb()</code>. These results are not compared with the table-based ones.</p>
</section>
{% if parquet_left_out %}
<p class="note">Left out of the common Parquet query set:
  {% for e in parquet_left_out %}{{ e.label }} ({{ e.reason }}){{ "; " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}. Their own totals are still shown.</p>
{% endif %}
{{ chart("trackb_total", "Total query time over Parquet, common queries (s)", "Sum of warm medians over the queries every entry point ran correctly.", 320) }}
{{ chart("trackb_query", "Per-query time over Parquet (s, log scale)", "Same layout as above. The join item exists only for VillageSQL (its documented pattern).", 460, true) }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}{% if not empty %}{% include "_data.html.j2" %}{% endif %}{% endblock %}
